@startuml arch-checkpoint-state
' The two state machines that make a crash survivable: a PREFIX's lifecycle (tracked
' in the global ImportCheckpoint) and a SHARD's sync lifecycle (ShardSyncCoordinator).
' Each is a live TLA+ model — the red notes name the machine-checked invariants.
' Colour legend (semantic, shared across all repo diagrams — see architecture.puml):
'   #1565C0 blue = in-flight / statistical core   #2E7D32 green = durable, terminal-good
'   #00838F teal = storage / persistence          #EF6C00 orange = error states
'   #546E7A grey = not-yet-started                #C62828 red = formal verification
' Render: plantuml -tsvg docs/diagrams/arch-checkpoint-state.puml
' Source of truth for Figure 4 in docs/architecture/google-books-importer.md §5
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam ArrowColor #37474F
skinparam ArrowFontColor #37474F
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFEBEE
skinparam NoteBorderColor #C62828
skinparam state {
  BackgroundColor #ECEFF1
  FontColor #263238
  BorderColor #455A64
  FontStyle bold
  BackgroundColor<<init>> #546E7A
  FontColor<<init>> #FFFFFF
  BackgroundColor<<active>> #1565C0
  FontColor<<active>> #FFFFFF
  BackgroundColor<<store>> #00838F
  FontColor<<store>> #FFFFFF
  BackgroundColor<<durable>> #2E7D32
  FontColor<<durable>> #FFFFFF
  BackgroundColor<<error>> #EF6C00
  FontColor<<error>> #FFFFFF
}
title Crash-safety state machines — prefix lifecycle (left) · shard sync (right)

state "PREFIX  —  ImportCheckpoint,  one instance per (order, prefix)" as PrefixSM {
  state "NotStarted" as NS <<init>>
  state "InProgress" as IP <<active>>
  state "Completed" as CO <<durable>>
  state "Failed" as FA <<error>>

  [*] --> NS
  NS --> IP : start_prefix\n(a worker claims it)
  IP --> CO : commit_prefix_tx\n**data durable first**
  IP --> FA : stream or storage error
  FA --> IP : retry with backoff
  IP --> FA : **crash, then reopen**\nrecover_in_progress_as_failed
  CO --> [*]
}

note bottom of PrefixSM
  **CheckpointStateMachine.tla**  (TLC + TLAPS)
  · **DisjointSets** — a prefix sits in **exactly one** set, so it
    can never be counted twice.
  · **CrashRecoverySound** — every prefix recorded in-progress
    at the crash is, after restart, either still in-progress or
    Failed. Never silently Completed.
  · **NoDoubleProcessing** — Completed ∩ InProgress = ∅.
end note

state "SHARD  —  ShardSyncCoordinator,  an AtomicU8 driven by CAS" as ShardSM {
  state "Clean" as CL <<durable>>
  state "Dirty" as DI <<store>>
  state "Syncing" as SY <<active>>
  state "SyncFailed" as SF <<error>>

  [*] --> CL
  CL --> DI : first increment_cas\nmark_dirty (a **Clean-only** CAS)
  DI --> SY : try_start_sync\nCAS Dirty → Syncing — **elects the one syncer**
  SY --> CL : complete_sync(lsn)
  SY --> SF : fail_sync(err)
  SF --> DI : retry_sync
  DI --> DI : further writes\n(**already Dirty** — no transition)
  SY --> SY : writes **continue** during the sync\n(the snapshot is an immutable RCU point-in-time)
}

note bottom of ShardSM
  **AsyncShardSync.tla**  (TLC + TLAPS — 249 proof obligations)
  · **AtMostOneSyncer** — the Dirty → Syncing CAS means two
    checkpoint threads can never publish the same shard.
  · **CleanMeansZeroDirty** — Clean implies no unpublished write.
  · A write landing //during// Syncing is safe **by delegation**:
    libdictenstein's LockFreeDurableCheckpoint retains any
    post-watermark write in the WAL and replays it on reopen.
end note

@enduml
